nearly a month after they disappeared in  a cave in Thailand twelve soccer players  and their coach are going home at a news  conference this morning the boys all  wore their team uniforms as they spoke  about their experience for the first  time the players appear to be healthy  and in good spirits also at the news  conference Thai Navy SEALs involved in  their dramatic rescue Anna Warner is in  Chiang Rai Thailand  Anna good morning well good morning and  as you can see behind me here they are  the twelve soccer players and their  coach here in their first news  conference where they're talking about  their experiences in detail in the cave  there's a person questioning them here  in Thai as you can probably hear when  they first entered the room some people  applauded they had soccer balls right in  front of the stage and so the boys kind  of showed off their soccer moves they  bounced balls in the air  they all look healthy and health  officials say that they are healthy  mentally that they're healthy physically  they're doing well one of the doctors in  the beginning said well you can see how  strong they are they're in high spirits  and they are ready to face what he  called the normal world what we've been  hearing over these minutes now is the  what the kids talking about what it was  like for them for example for the first  night they said they weren't scared that  they wouldn't be found because it was  just the first night you know they kind  of where they were waiting for the water  to go down in the cave and they thought  that by the next day the water would  drop enough so that they could escape so  initially they weren't scared  I think they became more scared over  time and some of them talked about  encouraging the others not to give up  the coach I think was supporting them in  the cave in this but one of the problems  obviously and they were able to get  water that dripped off the cave walls  but they really didn't have any food one  of the kids here one of the younger kids  said that after a couple of days he  started to dream about food about his  favorite foods and that they became very  hungry so what we're hearing so far as  they're giving a very detailed in-depth  description of what it  like for them to be sort of in that cave  in the early moments they had to sort of  climb up onto that high slope within the  cave if you remember the first video  when the British divers found them you  could see they were kind of crouched  into this area a very limited amount of  space kind of on a high slope where they  were able to get out of the water and  they talked about in this news  conference they talked about how excited  they were when the British cave divers  first emerged from the water you could  almost kind of hear it here in their  voices a little bit obviously they're  speaking Thai we're getting an English  translation but you could kind of hear  in their voices how excited they were  and I think it's fair to say that the  room is sort of listening to their every  word people want to hear every detail  this news conference is being broadcast  live across the entire country of  Thailand  on TV and on radio and it's probably  fair to say that most of the people in  Thailand right now I would bet they are  tuned in they are listening to this and  they are hanging on these kids every  word what a great story John thanks for  us so much thanks so much Anna and the  world won't be normal anymore for them  but wow what a story  jesse is remember he was here at the  table the guy who lives life to the  fullest doing all sorts of things says  this may sound crazy but these kids will  look on this years later and say that  was a cool adventure since it turned out  the way it did as a little boy when you  think about it that way you said okay  that's right a life experience so that  nobody else can share that's great
 

